ram (e.g., #100ragazzeSTEM, Disco Lazio, or thesis awards).\n• Prepare all documents early: academic transcripts, motivation letter, recommendation letters, and proof of language proficiency (Italian or English as required).\n• Apply as early as possible since deadlines are rolling and many funds are limited.\n• For accommodation and living cost support, check the LazioDiSco regional scholarship requirements separately.\n• Explore merit-based and need-based options together—some scholarships can be stacked if eligibility permits.	{Italy,"Sapienza University",Rome,Bachelor's,Master's,PhD,"Tuition Waiver","Women in STEM"}	Sapienza University of Rome, one of Europe's oldest and most prestigious universities, offers a wide array of scholarships for international students, including Bangladeshis, in 2026. From full tuition waivers and living allowances to housing support through LazioDiSco, these opportunities cover almost every need. Whether you're pursuing a Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD, you can find funding that matches your profile—be it a merit-based award like 'Wanted the Best,' a regional grant for housing and healthcare, or the #100ragazzeSTEM scholarship encouraging women in STEM. The rolling deadlines mean you should start your application early, but the flexibility allows you to apply at any time. With additional support for student collaborations, thesis research, and even internships abroad, Sapienza is an excellent choice for Bangladeshi students seeking a world-class education in the heart of Rome.	A photorealistic image of the main entrance of Sapienza University of Rome at golden hour, with warm sunlight casting long shadows on the classical stone columns and arches. The sky is a mix of soft orange and pale blue, with a few wispy clouds. In the foreground, a cobblestone path leads to the grand doorway, flanked by lush green hedges. The mood is prestigious and welcoming, with deep gold and terracotta tones reflecting the university's history and prestige.